  "name": "IHC - ROUND CELL TUMOUR (ADULT OR PAEDIATRIC)",
  "code": "1694",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<h3 data-start=\"2894\" data-end=\"2910\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"2898\" data-end=\"2910\">Comments</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"2911\" data-end=\"3229\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2911\" data-end=\"3014\">\n<p data-start=\"2913\" data-end=\"3014\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Small round cell tumors are morphologically similar; hence, <strong data-start=\"2973\" data-end=\"2999\">IHC panel is essential</strong> for diagnosis.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"3015\" data-end=\"3132\">\n<p data-start=\"3017\" data-end=\"3132\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Clinical, radiological, and <strong data-start=\"3045\" data-end=\"3098\">molecular correlation (e.g., EWSR1 rearrangement)</strong> may be required for confirmation.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"3133\" data-end=\"3229\">\n<p data-start=\"3135\" data-end=\"3229\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Consider referral for <strong data-start=\"3157\" data-end=\"3180\">FISH / RT-PCR / NGS</strong>, especially for translocation-associated tumors.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
